Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:29:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11254/11362] Record reviewer findings 5-9; promote the
 cross-level residual to a finding

The reviewer filed one item under "what checks out" as a residual asymmetry:
enabled_arms_for_entry unions arms fired anywhere in the run, so an arm fired on
level 5 raises the exhaustion bar for level 2. That is cross-level reasoning
inside a change whose whole subject is removing cross-level reasoning -- the same
species as finding 1. Conservative in direction is not the same as on the right
axis, so it is recorded as finding 9 rather than a footnote, with the reviewer
asked to correct the reading if it is wrong.

Finding 7's handling is recorded as a habit to copy rather than as a defect. The
mutation numbering skips M14; the reviewer established the count was internally
consistent -- fifteen entries, backups matching, no log reference -- and reported
the gap anyway, because an unexplained gap has the same shape as a dropped
survivor. Verifying something is probably fine and reporting it regardless is the
right disposition for that anomaly.

